  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": "# ML-10 — Content Action Playbook\n\nThis skeleton is yours to fill. Work the sections **in order** — each one has a one-line hint. Simple words, honest numbers.\n\n> Working with an AI assistant? Tell it to read `skills/README.md` first and load the one skill this assignment names on its card."
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": "## 1. Ranked actions + reason codes\n\n*The queue: what to do first, and why, in words a human trusts.*"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": "import pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nif 'df' not in globals():\n    try:\n        from datasets import load_dataset\n        df = load_dataset(\"FlyRank/internship-starter\", split=\"train\").to_pandas()\n    except Exception:\n        raise RuntimeError(\"Load df first from the starter dataset, then rerun.\")\n\noutdir = Path(\"work/outputs\")\nfigdir = Path(\"work/figures\")\noutdir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\nfigdir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n\n# ranked actions and reason codes from validated signals\nscore = (\n    100 * df.get('needs_indexing', False).astype(int) +\n    80 * df.get('needs_ctr_fix', False).astype(int) +\n    60 * df.get('is_quick_win', False).astype(int) +\n    40 * df.get('is_declining', False).astype(int) +\n    20 * df['freshness_tier'].eq('0-30').astype(int)\n)\n\nreason_code = np.select(\n    [df.get('needs_indexing', False), df.get('needs_ctr_fix', False), df.get('is_quick_win', False), df.get('is_declining', False)],\n    ['INDEXING', 'CTR_FIX', 'QUICK_WIN', 'DECLINE'],\n    default='ROUTINE'\n)\n\naction_label = np.select(\n    [df.get('needs_indexing', False), df.get('needs_ctr_fix', False), df.get('is_quick_win', False), df.get('is_declining', False)],\n    ['FIX_INDEXING', 'FIX_CTR', 'QUICK_WIN_REFRESH', 'REFRESH'],\n    default='REVIEW'\n)\n\nqueue = df[['content_id', 'client_id']].copy()\nqueue['score'] = score\nqueue['reason_code'] = reason_code\nqueue['action_label'] = action_label\nqueue = queue.sort_values(['score', 'content_id'], ascending=[False, True]).reset_index(drop=True)\n\ndisplay(queue.head(15))\nqueue.to_csv(outdir / 'w07_ranked_queue.csv', index=False)\n\nprint('Ranked actions: FIX_INDEXING, FIX_CTR, QUICK_WIN_REFRESH, REFRESH, REVIEW')\nprint('Reason codes: INDEXING, CTR_FIX, QUICK_WIN, DECLINE, ROUTINE')"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": "## 2. Intended use and limits\n\n*Who uses this, for what — and where it stops being valid.*"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": "intended_use = pd.DataFrame([\n    ['primary_user', 'Content strategist or SEO analyst'],\n    ['use', 'Prioritize pages for human review and action planning'],\n    ['decision_type', 'Decision-support, not automatic publishing or editing'],\n    ['valid_when', 'Signals and traffic patterns are similar to the audited dataset'],\n    ['stops_being_valid', 'If data collection changes, labels shift, or client behavior changes materially'],\n], columns=['item', 'value'])\n\ndisplay(intended_use)\n\nprint('This playbook is for queue ordering and human planning.')\nprint('It is not a production auto-action system.')\nprint('It should be used only on similar, audited data and rechecked when the data regime changes.')"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": "## 3. Human review + the no-go list\n\n*What a person must check before acting. What should never be automated.*"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": "review_rules = pd.DataFrame([\n    ['check_action', 'A human confirms the action matches the page and reason code.'],\n    ['check_context', 'A human checks whether the page has a known campaign, seasonality, or manual edit.'],\n    ['check_priority', 'A human can override the queue for business-critical pages.'],\n    ['check_confidence', 'Low-confidence rows stay in review, not automatic action.'],\n], columns=['rule', 'human_review'])\n\nno_go = pd.DataFrame([\n    ['auto_publish', 'Do not automatically publish or overwrite content.'],\n    ['auto_delete', 'Do not automatically delete pages or content.'],\n    ['auto_client_comm', 'Do not automatically message clients or stakeholders.'],\n    ['auto_budget_shift', 'Do not automatically shift budgets or bids.'],\n    ['auto_label_creation', 'Do not create new labels from future outcomes.'],\n], columns=['no_go', 'why'])\n\ndisplay(review_rules)\ndisplay(no_go)\n\nprint('Human review is required before any action is taken.')\nprint('No-go: automatic publishing, deletion, client messaging, budget shifts, or any future-label automation.')"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": "## 4. Monitoring / retrain triggers\n\n*What would tell you the recommendations went stale?*"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": "monitoring = pd.DataFrame([\n    ['queue_drift', 'The mix of reason codes changes a lot from the audited baseline.'],\n    ['metric_drop', 'Human-reviewed success rate falls after rollout.'],\n    ['feature_shift', 'CTR, freshness, or position distributions move materially.'],\n    ['label_shift', 'The meaning or source of the target changes.'],\n    ['client_shift', 'A new client mix or domain mix appears.'],\n], columns=['trigger', 'why_it_matters'])\n\ndisplay(monitoring)\n\nprint('Retrain or rebuild the playbook if the queue drifts, the human-reviewed outcome drops, or the data regime changes.')\nprint('Use light monitoring: weekly reason-code share, approval rate, and basic feature drift checks.')"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": "## 5. Exports for the paper\n\n*Write the queue (and any figures you want to reuse) to work/outputs/ — your paper builds on these files.*"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": "# exports for the paper\nqueue.to_csv(outdir / 'w07_ranked_queue.csv', index=False)\n\n# metrics receipts for traceability\nreceipts = pd.DataFrame([\n    ['rows_ranked', len(queue)],\n    ['top_score', int(queue['score'].max())],\n    ['unique_reason_codes', queue['reason_code'].nunique()],\n], columns=['metric', 'value'])\nreceipts.to_json(outdir / 'w07_playbook_receipts.json', orient='records', indent=2)\n\n# a small figure for reuse\ntry:\n    import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n    fig = plt.figure(figsize=(8, 4))\n    queue['reason_code'].value_counts().sort_values(ascending=True).plot(kind='barh')\n    plt.title('Ranked queue by reason code')\n    plt.xlabel('count')\n    plt.tight_layout()\n    figpath = figdir / 'w07_reason_code_mix.png'\n    plt.savefig(figpath, dpi=160, bbox_inches='tight')\n    plt.close(fig)\n    print(f'Saved figure: {figpath}')\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f'Figure export skipped: {e}')\n\nprint('Exports written to work/outputs/ and work/figures/.')"
    },
    {
